jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.33~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * No existence check decides its answer by reading the words an array
    chose. Three of them did: PowerFlex volume_get and volume_id_by_name,
    and PowerVault volume_get_by_name, all matching /not found/. An array
    saying "storage pool not found" about a wrong pool would have been read
    as "this volume is gone" - and the caller's next move is to create a
    second one.
  * They use the status code now (REST gained get_or_undef and the
    allow_status option), or they ask a question that answers itself: on
    PowerVault a pattern listing that succeeds without the name in it is
    proof, and if the listing fails too the original error is raised rather
    than guessed at.
  * t/11-imports.t fails on any new decision made by matching an array's
    error text, so this cannot come back quietly. It is the third time in
    this project.

