jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.28~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * PowerFlex: a volume mapped to an NVMe host could have looked unmapped
    forever. A mapping entry names its target as an SDC id or a host id, and
    an entry may carry both; the code took whichever was defined first and
    dropped the other. A node that goes by its host id would have found the
    volume unmapped on every activation, mapped it again, and later unmapped
    it by an id that was not the one holding it. Every id an entry names is
    now reported, and mappedHostInfo is read alongside mappedSdcInfo.
  * PowerVault: host lookup by name matches both spellings a row may carry
    rather than whichever is defined first. Same shape, same reason.
  * t/16-docs.t now also sees fields read through a variable. A qw() list of
    field names was invisible to it, which is how mappedHostInfo could have
    reached a release without a line in the table.

