jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.27~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * PowerVault: the field order introduced in 0.7.26 is corrected. The
    column headings 'show volumes' prints - Total Size, Alloc Size - are not
    the property names the JSON carries. The volumes basetype documents
    size, total-size and allocated-size, each with a -numeric twin in
    512-byte blocks, so those lead again and the headings are kept only as
    later fallbacks. Nothing broke in 0.7.26 because the fallback chain
    covered it; the order was simply wrong about which name is documented.
  * The snapshot timestamp field creation-date-time-numeric is no longer
    marked unverified: the volumes basetype documents it.
  * docs/TESTING.md states the distinction plainly, because it is what made
    the guess wrong: a printed column heading is not a property name.

