jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.26~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * PowerVault: the second volume mapped to a host would have collided with
    the first. next_free_lun compared the host against whichever identity
    field a mapping row defined first, and a real row defines both - so the
    initiator IQN was compared against a host name, no row ever matched, and
    every LUN looked free. It now matches any of the identities a row
    carries, and does so without regard to case.
  * PowerVault: volume size and used space read the field names the CLI
    Reference documents. 'show volumes' names its columns Total Size and
    Alloc Size; the code looked for Size and Allocated Size first, so used
    space read as zero on an array that spells it as documented. The older
    spellings are still accepted behind the documented ones.
  * The comment claiming 'show maps' has no host-name column was wrong: the
    volume-view-mappings basetype documents nickname as the host or host
    group name. It is blank when unset, which is why the initiator id is
    still matched too.
  * docs/TESTING.md records the show volumes output columns, the
    volume-view-mappings and initiator-view properties, and that the pattern
    parameter takes shell wildcards and matches names containing the string.

