jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.25~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * PowerStore: 416 Range Not Satisfiable while paging a collection no longer
    fails the whole listing. Dell documents 416 as the answer to an offset
    past the end, and paging reaches one legitimately when a volume is
    deleted on another node between pages - the total came from the first
    page. A concurrent delete would have made the storage report itself
    broken.
  * PowerStore: the iSCSI portal lookup no longer depends on the 'cs' filter
    operator being accepted. If the filtered query finds nothing, every
    address is fetched and the Storage_Iscsi_Target purpose matched locally.
    An operator the array reads differently would have meant no portals, no
    iSCSI login and no devices at all - with nothing in the logs to say why.
  * The REST layer gained allow_status, so a caller that knows what a
    particular refusal means can act on the status code rather than on the
    wording of the array's message.
  * docs/TESTING.md records the pagination rules read from the developers
    guide: limit 1 to 2000 (default 100), offset, the Range header, 206 with
    Content-Range, and 416 for an offset past the end.

