jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.17~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * PowerVault checked whether a host already had this node's initiator by
    reading flat fields on the host object. 'show host-groups' nests the
    initiators inside the host, so the check always said no, and every host
    check would have re-added a member the array already had — a refusal
    there fails activate_storage, so a working storage would have gone
    inactive. The id is now looked for anywhere within the host structure,
    whatever the firmware nests it in, and a refusal that means "it is
    already how you want it" is accepted.
  * iSCSI ports the array reports as Not Present, Disconnected or in Error
    are no longer offered to the login loop. 'show ports' documents Media,
    Target ID — the node name for an iSCSI port — Status, IP Address and
    Health; only Media and the address were being read.
  * The tolerated-refusal check matches the array's own words only. The
    rendered error also carries the command, and a command named
    'add host-members' matches any pattern looking for the word 'member' —
    the same trap that made template deletion impossible in 0.7.12.

