jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.14~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * PowerVault would not have come up at all. Two commands on the first
    activation of the storage were guesses, and both were wrong:
      - creating a host is 'create host initiators <list> <name>', not
        'create host id <list> <name>';
      - attaching an initiator to an existing host is 'add host-members
        initiators <list> <host>'. What was there, 'set initiator host ...',
        is a different command that names an initiator and attaches it to
        nothing, and the syntax was not valid either.
    Both are now as the ME4/ME5 CLI Reference Guide documents them, and every
    missing initiator goes in one command instead of one each.
  * Four other PowerVault commands were checked against the same guide and
    found correct as written: delete volumes, set volume name, unmap volume,
    and the size and name limits. docs/TESTING.md records which are now read
    from documentation rather than inferred.

