  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * New test t/17-lifecycle.t walks a whole VM's life against an array that
    refuses what a real one refuses — deleting a volume that still has
    snapshots, deleting a snapshot something was cloned from, creating a name
    that already exists — and checks after every step that the array holds
    exactly what it should and that nothing was left behind.
  * It found a misleading error: deleting a template that still has a linked
    clone reported "the volume still has snapshots", because that was the
    array's answer about the volume. The array's answer about the SNAPSHOT
    said the useful thing — it has dependent clones — and that is now carried
    into the message the operator sees.

