jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.9~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * pve-dell-config-get's --insecure flag did nothing: both branches of the
    expression behind it produced the same value. Certificate verification is
    off by default in recover mode, which matches the plugin's own default and
    is what recovery against a self-signed certificate needs; --verify-ssl now
    turns it on, and both flags also apply when the details come from
    storage.cfg.
  * A protection domain named in pflex-protection-domain is now a requirement
    rather than a tie-breaker. It was only consulted when the pool name was
    ambiguous, so a storage configured with a domain could still land on a
    pool in a different one — which is what naming the domain was meant to
    prevent.
  * An endpoint that manages more than one PowerFlex system says so rather
    than silently using whichever was listed first.
  * A REST client built without a type no longer produces an uninitialised
    value warning on top of whatever error it was reporting.
  * docs/TESTING.md now says where each unverified endpoint can be checked:
    PowerStore publishes Swagger UI on the array itself, and the PowerVault
    commands can be tried over SSH first.

